# Vendored upstream artifacts are hashed, so their bytes may not be rewritten.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the delivery machine, and without this git converts these files to
# CRLF on checkout. That changes their bytes, which changes their sha256, which makes
# `third-party/node/NODE_RUNTIME_PIN.json` disagree with the very files it pins — so a fresh clone
# would fail to build a distribution, with a licence-tamper message, on a repository nobody had
# touched. Caught by the staging warning rather than by the failure, which would have happened on
# somebody else's machine.
third-party/node/LICENSE -text
third-party/node/SHASUMS256.txt -text
